{"term":"instance","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:d9372067e7990f0065","definition":"Urgency of manner or words; an urgent request; insistence.","example":"I know one very well alied, to whom, at the instance of a brother of his[…], I spake to that purpose[…].","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["noninstance"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"countable, obsolete, uncountable","wordFamily":["argument instance","instance-based programming","instancy","instant","instantaneous","instantial","instantiate","instantiation","instantly","substitution instance","tribunal of first instance"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instance#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:bf39f3d33bac6ca579","definition":"A token; a sign; a symptom or indication.","example":"It sends some precious instance of itself/ After the thing it loves.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["noninstance"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"countable, obsolete, uncountable","wordFamily":["argument instance","instance-based programming","instancy","instant","instantaneous","instantial","instantiate","instantiation","instantly","substitution instance","tribunal of first instance"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instance#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:43e1668675f04d9ec1","definition":"That which is urgent; motive.","example":"The instances that second marriage move\nAre base respects of thrift, but none of love.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["noninstance"],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"countable, obsolete, uncountable","wordFamily":["argument instance","instance-based programming","instancy","instant","instantaneous","instantial","instantiate","instantiation","instantly","substitution instance","tribunal of first instan