ntiate","instantiation","instantly","substitution instance","tribunal of first instance"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instance#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:1d37b5e8873c7694d1","definition":"A dungeon or other area that is duplicated for each player, or each party of players, that enters it, so that each player or party has a private copy of the area, isolated from other players.","example":"As long as the most difficult instance you've tried is Gnomeregan, you're never going to be credible talking about 'difficult encounters'.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["noninstance"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["argument instance","instance-based programming","instancy","instant","instantaneous","instantial","instantiate","instantiation","instantly","substitution instance","tribunal of first instance"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instance#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dfb5ea334f4d4ce8bd","definition":"An individual copy of such a dungeon or other area.","example":"The instance is created for the group that enters it.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["noninstance"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":["argument instance","instance-based programming","instancy","instant","instantaneous","instantial","instantiate","instantiation","instantly","substitution instance","tribunal of first instance"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/instance#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:283dbeadde1324d0d8","definition":"An independent server on a decentralised social network, such as Mastodon.","example":"To collect the me